<speak>We can use late morning as a general scheduling preference and check your actual availability each time. For an in-person meeting, we can make the location and expected format clear in the invitation so you can plan the journey without uncertainty. If you would rather speak by telephone, that is also a workable format for a routine relationship conversation. There is no need to combine it with a digital support session or a correspondence update unless doing so genuinely suits you. Sometimes keeping the purposes separate makes each appointment shorter and easier to prepare for, even if it means having more than one diary entry.</speak>